# ARP / REC: a keyboard drawn on the page, and the OCT buttons: dim = usable, full = an octave offset is set
expectled OCT- 0
expectled OCT+ 0
tap ARP
expect view 4
wait 100
expectled OCT- 1
expectled OCT+ 1
tap OCT+
wait 100
expectled OCT+ 2
expectled OCT- 1
shot arp_oct_up.png
tap OCT-
tap OCT-
wait 100
expectled OCT- 2
expectled OCT+ 1
key 12 down
wait 100
shot arp_held.png
key 12 up
tap OCT+
wait 100
expectled OCT- 1
expectled OCT+ 1
# REC the same; the sequencer has none (one page of 16 steps), a 32-step clip does
tap REC
wait 100
expectled OCT- 1
tap SEQ
wait 100
expectled OCT- 0
# KEYS mode: rate, gate and octaves are greyed out and do nothing; in an arpeggio mode they work
tap ARP
tap ARP
tap ARP
expect view 4
expect arpmode 0
turn K2 1
expect arprate 0
turn K1 1
expect arpmode 1
turn K2 1
expect arprate 1
